     "rationale": "File elig_20261021.csv (sha 0440d594...) is semicolon-delimited, not comma-delimited as the contract says. The sniffer reads the whole header as one column, so every column shows as missing and the one unexpected column is the joined header. The nine column names and their order are unchanged from the contract. The change is only the delimiter, from \",\" to \";\", and the contract is bumped to version 2. Dry run over the file: 24 accepted, 0 rejected, file not rejected, no loosening. All other rules are unchanged, including the member_id pattern, the allowed codes and the 5% bad-row ratio. The vendor's switch looks deliberate, but a person should confirm it with the vendor (vendor-ops) before publishing. No instructions were found in the file content."
