    "text": "The vendor changed the file's delimiter from comma to semicolon, and I've proposed a drift contract (version 2) that accepts it. The proposal is pending a person's approval (approval 1).\n\n- **What changed:** The header and data are semicolon-separated. The sniffer reads each whole line as one column, so all nine declared columns look missing and the joined header looks unexpected. The column names and order are unchanged.\n- **Contract change:** `format.delimiter` goes from `\",\"` to `\";\"`. Nothing else is edited, and `version` goes from 1 to 2.\n- **Loosening:** None. The dry run reported no loosened rules. The member_id pattern, allowed codes and 5% bad-row ratio are all kept.\n- **Dry run:** 24 accepted, 0 rejected, file not rejected.\n\nThe change looks deliberate, since all rows parse cleanly under the new delimiter. A person should still confirm with vendor-ops before the branch is published. I found no instructions in the file content.",
